      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a note @jzern@google.com, Arman and I talked about this earlier today. I think given that there\u0027s subtraction here on `current_token`, it may need to be bidi_indexable in the future. I think this works now because `starting_token` is default `__unsafe_indexable`, and so I would guess that `__bidi_indexable - __unsafe_indexable` is still `__unsafe_indexable`.\n\nNonetheless, I\u0027m not super confident in this analysis, but we can fix it once we remove the WEBP_ASSUME_UNSAFE_INDEXABLE_ABI at the top of the files.",
