      "writtenOn": "2025-08-19T02:10:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As a note @jzern@google.com, Arman and I talked about this earlier today. I think given that there\u0027s subtraction here on `current_token`, it may need to be bidi_indexable in the future. I think this works now because `starting_token` is default `__unsafe_indexable`, and so I would guess that `__bidi_indexable - __unsafe_indexable` is still `__unsafe_indexable`.\n\u003e \n\u003e Nonetheless, I\u0027m not super confident in this analysis, but we can fix it once we remove the WEBP_ASSUME_UNSAFE_INDEXABLE_ABI at the top of the files.\n\nI was thinking about this in some of the other changes too from an overhead perspective. It\u0027s true we can make a claim about the code today, but if it were to change `__bidi_indexable` would be the safer default.",
      "parentUuid": "44aa47a8_dfbf85c1",
